TutorialText.Text               = [=[Hello! welcome to Yatta's Crazy Gui (or simply, Bluu.) To use this script, it is recommended to execute this the main game for all toggles and tabs to appear.

to start autofarming, you will first have to toggle the "autofarm" button, obviously.
When toggled on, this will automatically turn on recommended buttons like auto pickup, auto hide, auto buy, and many more.

In the main game, you can manage things like auto pick up blacklist, auto buy blacklist, auto use item triggers, and monster farm detector radius. (these things are located at the tab that I have never named before, so just call it "configuration" tab. It is usually below the ESPs tab, the one with the "monitor" or "tv" icon.)

If you're struggling to click toggles/buttons, etc. you can change the UI's size in the settings.

The ESPs tab lets you see players, twisteds, items, machines, and tendrils through walls. Each one can be toggled on or off separately. The labels also show extra info like a generator's completion status or a player's health and items, not just their name.

The Players tab is for your own character, stuff like Walk Speed, Fly, Anti-AFK, and Teleport Walk. If you're in restricted mode, Server Hop and Rejoin buttons show up there too.

The Progress tab tracks your healing stats for the run: heals used, items dropped or stolen, hits taken, and how many healing items you currently have.

If you ever accidentally close the GUI, tap the floating icon that shows up on your screen to bring it back.

You can save and load multiple configs from the settings tab. Just type a name, hit save, and you can load it back anytime, useful if you like switching between different setups.

Each toggle shows "On" or "Off" on it directly, plus red means off and green means on if you want a quick glance.

Tap the "?" button anytime if you want to see this tutorial again.

please report any errors/problems/bugs (or send a recommendation) in the "Feedback" tab.

thank you for using this script. it is very much appreciated]=]
